  "solution": "Logic : (1st number × 3rd number × 10) = 2nd number\n\nGiven : \n\n__\n \n• 4 - 200 - 5\n\n4 × 5 × 10__ = 200\n\n200 = 200 (LHS = RHS)\n\n__\n \n• 6 - 420 - 7\n\n6 × 7 × 10__ = 420\n\n420 = 420 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n__\n \n• Option - (1) : 3 - 660 - 9\n\n3 × 9 × 10__ = 660\n\n180 ≠ 660 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n__\n \n• Option - (2) : 7 - 780 - 8\n\n7 × 8 × 10__ = 780\n\n560 ≠ 780 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\n__\n \n• Option - (3) : 8 - 720 - 9\n\n8 × 9 × 10__ = 720\n\n**720 = 720 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n__\n \n• Option - (4) : 4 - 400 - 7\n\n4 × 7 × 10__ = 400\n\n280 ≠ 400 (LHS ≠ RHS)\n\nHence, \"Option - (3)\" is the correct answer.",
